<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_SentinelDefend.xml               UtinniPatches - SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2 build pass

  scarlands_kit_spec.md §4 (Forgotten Sentinels), owner ruling 6b (card
  sitting 2026-09-11, "Double them, then accept"): acquire 72 / keep 80 /
  wander 24 / defend 80 — supersedes the section's own first drafted 36/40/
  12/40.

  A clone of vanilla DutyDefOf.Defend (RimSage raw XML, quoted in full in
  SCARLANDS_MECHANICS_2.md's own header comment for RM_LordToil_
  DefendPerimeter.cs) with only the two JobGiver_AIFightEnemy-derived radii
  and the wander radius changed:

    - JobGiver_AIDefendPoint.targetAcquireRadius/targetKeepRadius are plain
      protected fields on the JobGiver, set straight from this DutyDef's XML
      (JobGiver_AIFightEnemy.cs, decompile-confirmed) — NOT read from
      PawnDuty.radius, so they must be authored here rather than left to
      RM_LordToil_DefendPerimeter's own duty.radius assignment.
    - JobGiver_WanderNearDutyLocation.wanderRadius likewise a plain field on
      that JobGiver, tightened 8 -> 24 (the owner's ruling is a widening
      here, not the "8" vanilla default — 24 is a strongpoint holding formation,
      not a squad's tight leash).
    - defend RADIUS (80) is NOT a DutyDef field at all — that one lives on
      RM_LordJob_DefendPerimeter's own defendRadius, read into
      PawnDuty.radius by RM_LordToil_DefendPerimeter.UpdateAllDuties and
      consumed by JobGiver_AIDefendPoint.TryFindShootingPosition's
      maxRangeFromLocus. Nothing to duplicate here.

  ThinkNode_ForbidOutsideFlagRadius.maxDistToSquadFlag (16) is left at
  vanilla's own value — the spec's owner ruling names acquire/keep/wander/
  defend explicitly and no fifth number; changing this too would be
  invention past what was ruled.

  Consumed by RUT_LordJob_SentinelDefend.cs (RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards)
  via DefDatabase<DutyDef>.GetNamedSilentFail — no MayRequire needed on this
  def itself (DutyDef, JobGiver_* and ThinkNode_* classes are all vanilla),
  though the spawner building that assigns this duty lives behind
  mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards.
-->
<Defs>

  <DutyDef>
    <defName>RUT_SentinelDefend</defName>
    <alwaysShowWeapon>true</alwaysShowWeapon>
    <thinkNode Class="ThinkNode_Priority">
      <subNodes>
        <li Class="JobGiver_TakeCombatEnhancingDrug">
          <onlyIfInDanger>true</onlyIfInDanger>
        </li>
        <li Class="JobGiver_AIDefendPoint">
          <targetAcquireRadius>72</targetAcquireRadius>
          <targetKeepRadius>80</targetKeepRadius>
        </li>
        <li Class="ThinkNode_ForbidOutsideFlagRadius">
          <maxDistToSquadFlag>16</maxDistToSquadFlag>
          <subNodes>
            <li Class="ThinkNode_Subtree">
              <treeDef>SatisfyBasicNeedsAndWork</treeDef>
            </li>
          </subNodes>
        </li>
        <li Class="JobGiver_WanderNearDutyLocation">
          <wanderRadius>24</wanderRadius>
          <locomotionUrgencyOutsideRadius>Sprint</locomotionUrgencyOutsideRadius>
        </li>
      </subNodes>
    </thinkNode>
  </DutyDef>

</Defs>
